---
<BlogPost
  title="Dairy Queen Birthday Party Guide: Cake, Treats & Budget"
  description="Plan a Dairy Queen birthday party for 10, 15, 20 or 30 kids: which DQ cake to order, what it costs with cones or kids meals, timing and serving tips."
  h1="How to Plan a Dairy Queen Birthday Party (and What It Costs)"
  crumb="DQ Birthday Party Guide"
  eyebrow="DQ cakes and parties"
  image="/Images/dq-sheet-cake.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen sheet cake decorated for a party"
  datePublished="2026-10-24"
  dateModified="2026-10-24"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="lead"><strong>A Dairy Queen birthday party for 10 kids costs about $41 for an 8-inch DQ cake and a Kids’ cone each, or about $73 with a kids meal for every child.</strong> For 20 kids, a sheet cake and cones come to about $81. Below are the cake sizes, a budget for each party size, and a timeline so the cake is still frozen when you sing.</p>

  <p>All prices are typical U.S. prices from our own checks. Each DQ franchise sets its own prices, so use these for planning and confirm with your store.</p>

  <h2 id="cake-size">Step 1: Pick the cake size</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Up to 10 guests:</strong> an <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-8inch">8-inch round</a>, about $22.99.</li>
    <li><strong>12–16 guests:</strong> a <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-10inch">10-inch round</a>, about $32.99.</li>
    <li><strong>20–25 guests:</strong> a <a href="/items/dq-sheet-cake">sheet cake</a>, about $44.99. Dairy Queen lists it as serving 20 to 25.</li>
    <li><strong>30–40 guests:</strong> a sheet cake plus a 10-inch round, about $77.98.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Kids’ slices are usually smaller, so you can plan toward the top of each range. Count the adults too: they almost always want a slice. All sizes and flavors are in our <a href="/categories/dq-cakes">DQ cake prices guide</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="flavor">Step 2: Classic or Blizzard cake?</h2>
  <p>For a kids’ party, the classic chocolate-and-vanilla cake is the safe choice. It has no nuts or candy pieces and is the cheapest. A <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard-cake">Oreo Blizzard Cake</a> costs about $5.75 more in the 10-inch size and is the most popular upgrade. Skip the Reese’s cake if any guest has a peanut allergy, and check our <a href="/blog/dq-gluten-free-allergen-guide">DQ allergen guide</a> before you order.</p>

  <h2 id="budget">Step 3: Budget by party size</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Kids</th><th>Cake</th><th>Cake + Kids’ cone each</th><th>Cake + kids meal each</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{budgets.map((b) => <tr><td><strong>{b.kids}</strong></td><td>{b.cake}</td><td class="price-cell">{b.treatsOnly}</td><td class="price-cell">{b.withMeals}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The middle column adds a Kids’ vanilla cone (about $1.79) for every child. The last column adds a <a href="/categories/kids-meals">kids meal</a> (about $4.99) instead, which already includes a Kids’ cone, so you don’t need both. Taxes are not included.</p>
  <p>Want something cheaper than cones? <a href="/items/dilly-bar">Dilly Bars</a> are about $1.99 each and travel better, since they are wrapped and on a stick.</p>

  <h2 id="timeline">Step 4: Order on the right timeline</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1 week before:</strong> call your store if you need a sheet cake, two cakes, a photo cake or a specific Blizzard flavor, especially near holidays and graduation season.</li>
    <li><strong>48 hours before:</strong> the latest point for most custom cakes and sheet cakes.</li>
    <li><strong>Same day:</strong> a ready-made round cake from the freezer case. Staff can usually write a name and short message while you wait.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can order online or in the DQ app at participating stores. Add the birthday to your <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-app-rewards-hacks">DQ Rewards profile</a> too, since the app usually sends a birthday treat offer.</p>

  <h2 id="serving">Step 5: Transport and serve it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Bring a cooler or an insulated bag for the drive, and go straight home or to the venue.</li>
    <li>Keep the cake in the freezer until 10 to 15 minutes before cutting.</li>
    <li>Cut with a long knife dipped in warm water, wiping it between slices.</li>
    <li>Put leftovers back in the freezer right away, covered.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A slice of a classic 10-inch cake cut 14 ways is about 400 calories. A sheet cake cut 22 ways is about 385. More on slicing and flavors is in our <a href="/blog/dq-cakes-complete-guide">DQ cakes guide</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="at-dq">Having the party at Dairy Queen</h2>
  <p>Dairy Queen does not offer a national party package, but many franchise stores are happy to help with a group order or set aside a few tables at a quiet time. Call ahead, give a head count, and ask whether they can have the cake and cones ready when you arrive. Weekday afternoons are usually the easiest time.</p>
</BlogPost>
